  [RISK] lib/sbi/sbi_illegal_atomic.c:100-121  DEFINE_ATOMIC_FUNCTION
      The `while(fail)` LR/SC retry loop in DEFINE_ATOMIC_FUNCTION (lines 108-117) has THREE termination conditions: successful SC, remote store/AMO breaking reservation, AND trap-based termination (both LR and SC are executed in unprivileged mode via MPRV, and the M-mode `__sbi_expected_trap` handler records trap info, which is then checked after each LR/SC). This is stronger than the pure M-mode loops in riscv_locks.c and riscv_atomic.c. However, in steady-state operation with valid addresses, neither LR nor SC will trap, and M-mode interrupts are typically disabled during emulation. The trap path only provides forward progress for the address-fault case, not for pure contention. If SC fails repeatedly under multi-hart contention on valid addresses, the loop still has no timeout or bounded-retry counter, degrading to the same 2-of-5 termination condition set as the M-mode loops. All AMO instruction variants (amoadd, amoswap, amoxor, amoor, amoand, amomin, amomax, amominu, amomaxu) are generated from this single macro
