  [RISK] contrib/llvm-project/lldb/source/Plugins/Instruction/RISCV/EmulateInstructionRISCV.cpp:333-381  AtomicSequence
      LLDB debugger emulation of the constrained LR/SC loop pattern. Recognizes only the exact 4-instruction sequence: LR.{W,D} → B (BNE) to exit → SC.{W,D} → B (BNE) to entry. When matched, atomically skips the entire sequence by jumping to exit_pc, preventing debugger single-stepping from breaking the reservation. However, the pattern matcher has two limitations: (1) it only recognizes BNE for both branches — alternative comparand-check branches (e.g., BEQ with inverted logic) or retry branches using different conditions will not match, falling through to instruction-by-instruction stepping where each step may break the reservation, and (2) the single-pass fcmpset pattern (LR → BNE → SC → J) is not recognized, though this is less critical since fcmpset has no retry loop. If a non-standard constrained LR/SC loop pattern is not recognized, single-stepping through it in the debugger could cause the SC to perpetually fail (reservation broken by each step), creating an artificial forward-progress failure indistinguishable from a Zalrsc violation.
